      "stageRecord": "The Icelandic verb líkar means 'likes' or 'is pleasing to' and selects a dative experiencer and a theme. In the VP-internal-subject implementation adopted here, Mér is the experiencer in Spec-VP, while þessi bók is the theme complement of V. The demonstrative þessi occupies D, and bók projects NP. The verb assigns the experiencer inherent dative Case together with its theta-role; this dative does not make Mér an ordinary direct object. The theme receives its theta-role here, but its nominative Case is licensed by finite inflection at the next stage. The overt words are inserted in their supplied forms; líkar is treated as a whole inflected word rather than as separately pronounced stem and ending.",
