      "stageRecord": "Finite I projects above the existing VP. The verb raises from V to I, leaving a head trace, and the dative experiencer raises from Spec-VP to Spec-IP, leaving an A-trace. These movements start from the positions represented in the preceding stage. Spec-IP satisfies the clause's subject requirement without replacing the experiencer's inherent dative with nominative. The subject chain receives only the experiencer theta-role assigned in VP. This analysis adopts the Icelandic quirky-subject configuration in which finite I licenses structural nominative on the lower theme across VP: the dative subject does not consume that nominative licensing. The third-person singular nominative theme is compatible with the singular form líkar. This example alone does not distinguish nominative-controlled third-person singular agreement from a matching default form. I carries abstract finite features and has no separate pronunciation; the supplied whole-word verb is licensed there without morphological splitting.",
