      "stageRecord": "A declarative CP is built above IP. The finite I complex raises to C from its previously represented position, leaving an I trace. The dative subject moves from Spec-IP to Spec-CP, leaving an A′-trace in Spec-IP. These independent extensions produce the canonical subject-initial V2 order: Mér is the first constituent and líkar occupies the second-position finite head. The subject's passage through Spec-IP remains represented, so its final position is not mistaken for evidence that it originated as an object. The linked subject dependencies preserve the single experiencer theta-role and inherent dative Case; the theme stays inside VP with nominative Case. Head movement proceeds through I rather than skipping it, and the subject dependencies remain local and c-command their lower traces. No separate Binding Theory violation arises: Mér is a free personal pronoun, and the other DP does not bind it. The completed sentence is grammatical Icelandic, meaning 'I like this book.' Its dative subject and nominative theme are licensed by the lexical and finite-clause properties represented here, not by silently changing either form.",
